{"text": " You wake up in 1500 in London. It is mid-summer eve, the shortest night of the year, and the streets are glowing with firelight. Did you know that almost everyone you will ever meet believes the sun goes around the earth? It is what Ptolemy taught about 1400 years ago. Your day begins when the sun rises and ends when it sets. But tonight nobody sleeps. Every door is hung with green birch and yellow flowers. Glass lamps burn old night, neighbors share bread and drink beside the bonfires. A London writer John Stowe later explained why a great fire he wrote could purge the infection of the air. Far away, a young Polish astronomer named Copernicus is studying the sky. In 1543, the year he dies, his book puts the sun at the center. And within 70 years, a new instrument will show that the sun is not perfect.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 1.82, "text": " You wake up in 1500 in London.", "tokens": [50364, 509, 6634, 493, 294, 22671, 294, 7042, 13, 50506], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15478521777737525, "compression_ratio": 1.5972222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 0.016544105485081673, "words": [{"word": " You", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.14, "probability": 0.783015787601471}, {"word": " wake", "start": 0.14, "end": 0.28, "probability": 0.9954946041107178}, {"word": " up", "start": 0.28, "end": 0.48, "probability": 0.9992932081222534}, {"word": " in", "start": 0.48, "end": 0.6, "probability": 0.9956739544868469}, {"word": " 1500", "start": 0.6, "end": 1.16, "probability": 0.7330198884010315}, {"word": " in", "start": 1.16, "end": 1.6, "probability": 0.9833335280418396}, {"word": " London.", "start": 1.6, "end": 1.82, "probability": 0.9939321875572205}]}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 2.88, "end": 5.28, "text": " It is mid-summer eve, the shortest night of the year,", "tokens": [50506, 467, 307, 2062, 12, 82, 30906, 34225, 11, 264, 31875, 1818, 295, 264, 1064, 11, 50656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15478521777737525, "compres